From d5212711b9cb0f7ed434de426a71316ca6a459ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.it>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 15:02:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 36/69] iommu/arm-smmu-qcom: Don't enable PRR on the SM7250
 Adreno SMMU

Like SM8250, the SM7250 Adreno SMMU does not implement the GFX PRR
registers. Writing ARM_SMMU_GFX_PRR_CFG_LADDR never completes, so
creating the first per-process pagetable (on the first GPU client's
first ioctl) leaves a CPU stalled with interrupts unserviced. Exclude
SM7250 the same way as SM8250.

This patch was generated by an AI coding assistant (Claude Opus 5.5 in
Claude Code) during an interactive bring-up session on a Motorola Moto G
5G Plus (XT2075-3, "nairo"). It has not yet been reviewed line by line
by a human and needs that review before any submission.

Assisted-by: LLM dtschema
---
 drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
index 795e8ec7e..55071eb03 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
@@ -394,6 +394,7 @@ static int qcom_adreno_smmu_init_context(struct arm_smmu_domain *smmu_domain,
 	priv->set_prr_addr = NULL;
 
 	if (of_device_is_compatible(np, "qcom,smmu-500") &&
+	    !of_device_is_compatible(np, "qcom,sm7250-smmu-500") &&
 	    !of_device_is_compatible(np, "qcom,sm8250-smmu-500") &&
 	    of_device_is_compatible(np, "qcom,adreno-smmu")) {
 		priv->set_prr_bit = qcom_adreno_smmu_set_prr_bit;
